{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T15:40:30.431Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"acquireLock and acquireLockLease refuse with code lock_path_unsafe when the tracker's locks directory or any component between the tracker root and the lock entry is a symlink or not a directory, or the lock entry itself is a symlink, and no file is created outside the tracker; A swap of the locks directory between the confinement check and lock creation is detected by comparing the created lock's identity with the confined directory entry, and the acquisition refuses with lock_path_unsafe (lock_directory_replaced) without ever deleting outside the tracker, leaving the stray lock in place and saying so in context.required; Regression tests cover a pre-existing symlinked locks directory and a swap during acquisition for both acquireLock and acquireLockLease, and the refusal is documented in docs/SDK.md"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T15:40:30.431Z"}],"before_hash":"08fcb627b246c613d494710da58293b08d335d775be805d1c12681a8034b7cc3","after_hash":"fec8b18f43b3a7da7216eba3a4d1aa3e5ee0e5b43389ec8906b9b84831976932","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f1518356283e06a84e8ea2b37d1eec2ef78bec429d07107d99f2c9a2b67bd64f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T15:40:42.401Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Confinement specs pass for a pre-existing symlink (both entrypoints), a regular-file locks entry (all platforms), a symlinked entry with per-reason recovery text, a swap during acquisition leaving the stray lock outside untouched, a swap-back that preserves a peer lock, a symlinked tracker root, and the gc refusal. Lock unit tests, the full suite and 100% coverage pass."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"New core/lock/lock-confinement.ts: lstat-walk of every component between tracker root and lock parent before mkdir or the cleanup gate (refuses lock_directory_symlink, lock_directory_not_directory, lock_path_outside_tracker); a symlinked lock entry refuses lock_entry_symlink; after open(wx) the handle dev/ino must equal lstat(lockPath) inside the same directory identity, else lock_directory_replaced. The refusal never unlinks lockPath and never deletes outside the tracker: the stray lock stays where the swap pointed and context.required says so per reason. pm gc --scope locks refuses a symlinked locks dir. Mid-operation swaps after the one-time check are tracked in pm-jd2zim. Documented in docs/SDK.md."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T15:40:42.401Z"}],"before_hash":"fec8b18f43b3a7da7216eba3a4d1aa3e5ee0e5b43389ec8906b9b84831976932","after_hash":"4062c3f1780d3a7b3b2d4fbf7d3bd810696f74a4135d3afe98d20ca7ce239d3a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a22822912f670316fdd3c4c2bb5bb34d25308e93e9db38c149da7b2654386284"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T15:40:43.055Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-01T15:40:43.055Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1648 review follow-up (CodeRabbit). Ordering note: gate_evidence was recorded after close and release (history entry 12) because the defect-evidence gate first failed on the hosted run; the evidence describes the shipped fix and its guards and is recorded as a follow-up instead of rewriting the append-only history. Behavior change: the lock_directory_replaced refusal no longer removes the stray lock through /proc/self/fd plus a path unlink, because the unlink cannot be bound to the identity check and could delete a same-name replacement outside the tracker; the stray lock now stays where the swap pointed, the never-released context.stray_lock_removed field is gone, and context.required branches per reason (lock_entry_symlink names the entry to remove, lock_directory_replaced explains the leftover). docs/SDK.md now says the lock entry refuses only as a symlink, scopes the nothing-outside claim to the four check-time reasons, and lists readSettingsSection and writeSettingsSection in the host contract. The regular-file case moved out of the symlink-only gate so Windows runs it. Pre-existing mid-operation swap windows (gc sweep, post-EEXIST reclaim, post-create entry check against a hard link, lstat failures treated as absent) are filed as pm-jd2zim."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T15:40:43.055Z"}],"before_hash":"4062c3f1780d3a7b3b2d4fbf7d3bd810696f74a4135d3afe98d20ca7ce239d3a","after_hash":"cf5010d598381ca713e66376d7bba6aaf166d178abd5cd46fd54256f60456018","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1beab179caa18db27f47097d20286da492de665fd310ca6d295d11047fbb02e7"}
